    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n1 1\n1\n2 2\n1 2\n3 4\n2 2\n1 3\n2 4\n1 5\n1 3 2 5 4\n3 3\n4 1 3\n9 2 6\n5 7 8",
        "output": "2\n5\n4\n3\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nFor the first test case, the grid is already sorted and no swaps are required. Hence, the grid can be sorted for the maximum possible value of XXX, and the beauty is 222.\n\n\nFor the second test case, the grid is already sorted. Since no swaps are needed, the grid remains sortable for the maximum possible value of XXX, so the beauty is 555.\n\n\nFor the third test case, one of the possible ways to sort the grid with X=4X = 4X=4:\n\nSwap the cells (1,2)(1,2)(1,2) and (2,1)(2,1)(2,1). Here, (∣1−2∣+1)⋅(∣2−1∣+1)=2⋅2=4(|1-2|+1)\\cdot(|2-1|+1) = 2 \\cdot 2 = 4(∣1−2∣+1)⋅(∣2−1∣+1)=2⋅2=4, which is ≥X\\ge X≥X. Hence, the swap is allowed.\nNow, grid is sorted."
      }
    ]
